# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for Clockwork's tests (CLOCKWORK_SANITIZE=thread).
#
# Rust is built with the stable toolchain, which cannot instrument for
# ThreadSanitizer, so the synchronisation inside the Rust subsystems — an
# Arc's reference count, a Mutex, a channel — is invisible to it. A C++ access
# ordered against a Rust thread by one of those reads as a race with no
# happens-before, however sound it is: the stream transport's connection
# writer dropped on its thread after the engine's send on another (an Arc,
# 2026-10-07, test_transports.cpp). Races with a Rust frame (a v0-mangled
# symbol) on one side are therefore not judged here. Everything on the C++
# side alone is, and a race between two C++ threads is never hidden by this.
#
# To judge the Rust side too: build it with a nightly toolchain and
# -Zsanitizer=thread, which this file would then make unnecessary.
race:^_RNv
race:^_R
